{
  "title": "Enterprise Observability Overview",
  "description": "Managed by Terraform (stacks/foundation). Is the platform itself healthy: coverage, ownership, alert quality, and the monitor budget. Per-domain and per-service views are Datadog-native (Service Catalog, APM, Infrastructure, the monitor list filtered by domain:) — see ADR-010.",
  "layout_type": "ordered",
  "reflow_type": "auto",
  "tags": ["team:observability-platform"],
  "template_variables": [
    { "name": "team", "prefix": "team", "default": "*" }
  ],
  "widgets": [
    {
      "definition": {
        "type": "note",
        "content": "## How to read this board\n\nThis is the platform grading itself. Coverage is easy to grow and easy to fake, so the top row is coverage and the four rows below it are the numbers that decide whether the coverage is worth anything:\n\n1. **Pages per week per team** — the burnout metric. Target < 5.\n2. **Alert volume by priority** — P1 should be rare and flat. A rising P1 line is either a real regression or a priority that has been devalued.\n3. **Noisiest monitors** — the review queue. Below grade C for two cycles is deletion, not discussion.\n4. **Predictive share** — how much of the estate uses anomaly/forecast/outlier detection rather than a number somebody guessed once.\n\nCoverage and click-ops metrics are published by `tools/coverage_report.py`; the full narrative lives in `generated/reports.md` (tools/reports.py). Nothing here drills into a single service — that is what the Service Catalog is for.",
        "background_color": "gray",
        "font_size": "14",
        "text_align": "left",
        "show_tick": false
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Coverage & governance gaps (must trend to zero)",
        "type": "query_value",
        "precision": 0,
        "requests": [
          {
            "queries": [
              {
                "data_source": "metrics",
                "name": "gaps",
                "query": "sum:acme.observability.coverage.gaps{report:latest}",
                "aggregator": "last"
              }
            ],
            "response_format": "scalar",
            "conditional_formats": [
              { "comparator": ">", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_red" },
              { "comparator": "<=", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_green" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Unowned resources (must be zero — 14 day SLA)",
        "type": "query_value",
        "precision": 0,
        "requests": [
          {
            "queries": [
              {
                "data_source": "metrics",
                "name": "unowned",
                "query": "sum:acme.observability.coverage.unowned{report:latest}",
                "aggregator": "last"
              }
            ],
            "response_format": "scalar",
            "conditional_formats": [
              { "comparator": ">", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_red" },
              { "comparator": "<=", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_green" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Unmanaged (click-ops) monitors — must be zero",
        "type": "query_value",
        "precision": 0,
        "requests": [
          {
            "q": "max:acme.observability.unmanaged_monitor_count{*}",
            "conditional_formats": [
              { "comparator": ">", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_red" },
              { "comparator": "<=", "value": 0, "palette": "white_on_green" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Managed monitor count against budget",
        "type": "query_value",
        "precision": 0,
        "requests": [
          {
            "q": "max:acme.observability.managed_monitor_count{*}",
            "conditional_formats": [
              { "comparator": ">", "value": 1500, "palette": "white_on_red" },
              { "comparator": ">", "value": 1200, "palette": "white_on_yellow" },
              { "comparator": "<=", "value": 1200, "palette": "white_on_green" }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Pages per team (7d) — the burnout metric",
        "type": "toplist",
        "requests": [
          {
            "q": "top(sum:datadog.monitor.alert_count{pages:true,managed_by:terraform} by {team}.as_count(), 10, 'sum', 'desc')",
            "style": { "palette": "warm" }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Alert volume by priority (30d)",
        "type": "timeseries",
        "requests": [
          { "q": "sum:datadog.monitor.alert_count{priority:p1,managed_by:terraform}.as_count()", "display_type": "bars" },
          { "q": "sum:datadog.monitor.alert_count{priority:p2,managed_by:terraform}.as_count()", "display_type": "bars" },
          { "q": "sum:datadog.monitor.alert_count{priority:p3,managed_by:terraform}.as_count()", "display_type": "bars" }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Noisiest monitors (30d) — the retuning and deletion queue",
        "type": "toplist",
        "requests": [
          {
            "q": "top(sum:datadog.monitor.alert_count{managed_by:terraform,$team.value} by {monitor_id}.as_count(), 20, 'sum', 'desc')",
            "style": { "palette": "orange" }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Detection mix — predictive vs fixed threshold",
        "type": "sunburst",
        "requests": [
          { "q": "sum:datadog.monitor.alert_count{managed_by:terraform} by {detection}.as_count()" }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "definition": {
        "title": "Estate by domain — open findings, all bands",
        "type": "manage_status",
        "summary_type": "groups",
        "display_format": "countsAndList",
        "color_preference": "background",
        "hide_zero_counts": true,
        "query": "tag:(managed_by:terraform) tag:($team.value)",
        "sort": "status,asc",
        "count": 50,
        "start": 0
      }
    }
  ]
}
